### Third-party code bundled by MuseScore: BeatRoot

The modules `crates/scoretk-midi-import/src/beatroot/` and
`beat_locator.rs` are Rust rewrites of the BeatRoot beat tracker that
MuseScore vendors under `src/importexport/midi/thirdparty/beatroot/`
(`Agent.{h,cpp}`, `AgentList.{h,cpp}`, `BeatTracker.{h,cpp}`, `Event.h`,
`Induction.{h,cpp}`, used by `importmidi_beat.cpp`):

- Original authors and copyright: **Simon Dixon, Chris Cannam and QMUL**
  (Centre for Digital Music, Queen Mary, University of London), 2011.
- Original licence: **GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your
  option) any later version** (`thirdparty/beatroot/COPYING`). It is
  redistributed here under GPL-3.0-only, which the "or later" clause
  permits.
- No C++ source is distributed: each Rust module carries the SPDX
  identifier and the porting notice naming its C++ counterpart.

The name conversion tables (`read302/tables.rs`, `read4xx/names.rs`)
follow `TConv::fromXml` of `engraving/rw/types/typesconv.cpp` — a file
**generated** at build time by MuseScore and therefore absent from the
reference copy — and the values of `engraving/types/types.h`.

## Code and behaviours reused from LilyPond

MuseScore 4 has no LilyPond export: the writer of `scoretk-lilypond-export` therefore does
not port any MuseScore C++ file for the output itself. Its
notation mappings (articulations, ornaments, dynamics, figures,
clef and key signature names, `\fixed` mode) follow the behaviour of
**`musicxml2ly`**, shipped with LilyPond.

- Originating project: **LilyPond**, <https://gitlab.com/lilypond/lilypond>.
- Licence: **GNU GPL version 3 or later** (GPL-3.0-or-later), Copyright
  (C) 2016--2026 John Gourlay, Werner Lemberg and the other authors of
  LilyPond. GPL-3.0-or-later permits distribution under GPL-3.0-only,
  the licence of this project.
- Nature of the reuse: **rewrite in Rust** of the observed tables and behaviour
  (`musicxml2ly` and `musicxml2ly_definitions.py`); no LilyPond file is
  distributed in this repository and no line of code is
  copied. The attribution also appears in the header of the relevant files of
  `crates/scoretk-lilypond-export/src/`.

### LilyPond reading (`crates/scoretk-lilypond-import/src/`)

The reader ports a subset of LilyPond's grammar. The reference
sources are a copy of **LilyPond 2.26.0**, commit
`3596756be0fac1f81066a99d2054329212172b2d`, kept outside the repository (for
example `../lilypond-ref/`, like `ref-musescore/`) and never distributed:

| Rust file | LilyPond source |
| --- | --- |
| `read/lexer.rs` | `lily/lexer.ll` (states `notes`, `lyrics`, `markup`, comments) |
| `read/parser.rs` | `lily/parser.yy` (`music_list`, `event_chord`, `chord_body`, `post_events`, `duration`, `repeated_music`, `context_change`, `\score`) |
| `read/pitch.rs` | `lily/pitch.cc` (`Pitch::to_relative_octave`, `steps`, `up_to`/`down_to`) and `scm/define-note-names.scm` (name tables by language) |
| `builder/articulate.rs` | `ly/articulate.ly` (`ac:trill`, `ac:articulate-chord`, actions `prall`, `mordent`, `turn`), file under GPL-3.0-only |
| `modes.rs` | `ly/drumpitch-init.ly` (`drumPitchNames`, `midiDrumPitches`) and `scm/chord-entry.scm` (`construct-chord-elements`): MIDI pitch tables for `\drummode` and `\chordmode` |
| `midi_instruments.rs` | `scm/midi.scm` (`instrument-names-alist`, `midi-program`, `percussion?`) and `lily/staff-performer.cc` (`new_instrument_string`): `midiInstrument` → GM program and channel 9 |

Licence: **GNU GPL version 3 or later**, Copyright (C) 1998--2026
Han-Wen Nienhuys and the other authors of LilyPond. The Rust rewrite
copies no line and is distributed under GPL-3.0-only, the project's licence.

**Scheme-free reader model**: `python-ly`
(<https://github.com/frescobaldi/python-ly>, GPL-3.0-or-later), consulted as
an architectural reference (`ly.music`, `ly.lex`) without reusing code. Its
licence is compatible with distributing this project under GPL-3.0-only.

Upgrade procedure: `docs/agents/lilypond.md` § 8 to § 10.

## Code and behaviours reused from xml2abc and abc2xml

MuseScore Studio has no native ABC import or export. The crates
`scoretk-abc-common`, `scoretk-abc-import` and `scoretk-abc-export`
follow the **ABC 2.1** standard
(<https://abcnotation.com/wiki/abc:standard:v2.1>) and the behaviour of the
scripts of **Willem Vree**:

- `xml2abc.py` (MusicXML → ABC), version **177**, `Copyright (C) 2012-2025:
  W.G. Vree`, downloaded on 2026-11-17 from
  <https://wim.vree.org/svgParse/xml2abc.html> ;
- `abc2xml.py` (ABC → MusicXML), version **269**, `Copyright (C) 2012-2026:
  Willem G. Vree`, downloaded on 2026-11-17 from
  <https://wim.vree.org/svgParse/abc2xml.html> ;
- their headers declare the « Lesser GNU General Public License as published
  by the Free Software Foundation », **without a version number**. LGPL 2.1
  § 3 permits conversion to GPL; distribution remains
  **GPL-3.0-only**.
- **Ported sources.** Since phase 1 of the ABC campaign (2026-11-19),
  `abc2xml.py` is a **ported source** on the same footing as MuseScore: the reader
  `crates/scoretk-abc-import/` reuses its function names and structure
  (`doNotations` for ties between different pitches, `long_decoration`
  / `linebreak` for recovering an orphan `!`; see the porting plan
  in `docs/agents/abc.md` § 16.4). `xml2abc.py` remains a source of
  behaviour for the writer (`crates/scoretk-abc-export/`). Both scripts
  are therefore declared here as **reused code and behaviours** (LGPL without
  a version number → GPL-3.0-only, LGPL 2.1 § 3), without any line being copied.
- Nature of the reuse: **rewrite in Rust** of the observed behaviour
  (`%%score` grammar, decorations, n-tuplets, lyrics, `K:` modes), without
  copying any line. No script of Willem Vree is distributed in this repository.
  The attribution also appears in the header of the files of
  `crates/scoretk-abc-common/src/` and in `docs/agents/abc.md` (§ 9 for the
  upgrade, § 16 for the port).

